From: Codex Unleashed <codex-unleashed@holdmyspot.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:30:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt released branding test fixtures to rust-v0.160.0

Retain the existing Unleashed welcome, status and connected-server warning
expectations. Include startup, voice-caption, status-copy and update fixtures.
Keep terminal colors consistent with the declared upstream base, reserve room
for the branded welcome header and address the directory row explicitly.

Account for branded root CLI argument ordering in exec-server help. Daemon
fixtures use a non-placeholder stable release and record the full branded
executable version in their package manifest. No production changes or new
daemon-updater feature work are included.

RED: maintained affected-package and workspace checks report the relevant
branding, version and startup-fixture failures; see final-emitted-packages.log
and fixture-final-workspace.log (exit100).
GREEN: existing focused compatibility gate passes 41/41 cases. The maintained
UI gate passes 196/197 with its one remaining stale accent expectation;
branding-halfwidth-green.log passes that corrected case (exit0). Additional
status-copy, remote-status, startup, ANSI, socket and native-audio checks pass
13/13 in branding-and-environment-additional.log (exit0). The other 196 checked
inputs remain unchanged. Maintained fmt-check passes (exit0).

Scope: test sources and terminal snapshots only. Snapshots intentionally
preserve rendered column padding; source whitespace checks exclude *.snap.
